# Maps with MapLibre

```elixir
Mix.install([{:kino_maplibre, "~> 0.1.13"}])

alias MapLibre, as: Ml
```

## A map

This notebook shows an interactive map with MapLibre, then pins a few cities on another. Drag the map, zoom it, and tilt it with the right mouse button.

```elixir
Ml.new(center: {19.94, 50.06}, zoom: 4)
|> Kino.MapLibre.add_nav_controls()
```

## Markers

Markers pin a few cities, and a layer of text names them.

```elixir
cities = [
  {"Kraków", {19.94, 50.06}},
  {"Berlin", {13.40, 52.52}},
  {"Paris", {2.35, 48.86}},
  {"Rome", {12.50, 41.90}}
]

markers = for {_name, location} <- cities, do: [location, color: "#ef7c00"]

names = %Geo.GeometryCollection{
  geometries:
    for {name, location} <- cities do
      %Geo.Point{coordinates: location, properties: %{name: name}}
    end
}

Ml.new(center: {10.0, 48.0}, zoom: 3)
|> Ml.add_geo_source("cities", names)
|> Ml.add_layer(
  id: "names",
  type: :symbol,
  source: "cities",
  layout: [text_field: ["get", "name"], text_font: ["Open Sans Semibold"], text_anchor: "top"]
)
|> Kino.MapLibre.add_markers(markers)
```
